Second Round:
Prompt:
Implementation Recovery Strategy
Scenario Brief: Prepare to outline your approach to engaging with a customer who has already begun their Service Cloud implementation but has stalled due to technical and adoption hurdles and now requires expert intervention.

 A customer attempted a self-implementation of Service Cloud to manage their technical support wing. It has been 4 months, the budget is exhausted, and the implementation is deemed "unusable" by the front line. The VP of Support is frustrated. She has a line of "Hiring Requests" on her desk and is 30 days away from pulling the plug on Salesforce to fund more headcount.

What are we looking for:
Your approach to understanding and resolving the technical issues
How would you figure out what went wrong
How will you earn the trust of this customer (VP, Admin, users) who at this point are defensive and convince them to move forward with a pilot

